In article <1170@xroads.UUCP> jerry@xroads.UUCP (Jerry M. Denman) writes:
> I am having trouble compiling Nethack under SCO Unix 3.2.2 with the
> 3.2.0 Dev system.  
>
> The most brutal of the errors is from obj.h concerning the struct obj.
>
> Anyone have diffs or help with this?

Whew! I'm glad you pointed this out. When I got this message, I suspected
my `C' wizardry had been drained by a wand of cancellation. :-)  After
all, NetHack is supposed to be machine independent. You'd have to be
stupid to have problems compiling it, right?

I had the same problem on the same type of system. Apparently, one of the
include files has `obj' defined: I tried compiling with `cc', `rcc', and
`gcc' and none of them worked. Then, I changed the name of all the `obj'
structures (boy, was *that* fun) and it compiled just fine.

Anyway, this really should be changed in the distribution source so that
we SCO (yuk!) people don't have these problems.

